{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.WeightDecompositionExists","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.WeightDecompositionExists","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Category.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Preadditive.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.NatTrans","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Defs"],"declarations":22,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WeightDecomposition.ofMaximalTorus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WeightDecomposition.ofMaximalTorus","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/weight-decomposition-exists.lean#L87-L112","doc":"**Existence of weight decomposition**.\n\nGiven a maximal torus acting on `Ω^k(A)`, the torus averaging\noperator constructs complementary idempotent projections `π_H`\n(weight-0) and `π_V` (non-zero weight), yielding a\n`WeightDecomposition`.\n\nThe construction:\n1. The averaging operator `e₀ = ∫_T ρ(t) dt` over the compact\n   torus is the weight-0 idempotent (Schur orthogonality).\n2. Set `π_H := e₀` and `π_V := id − e₀`.\n3. Complementarity holds by construction: `π_H + π_V = id`.\n4. Idempotency of `π_V` follows from `comp_idem_of_sum_id`.\n\nRef: [lusztig1993] https://doi.org/10.1007/978-0-8176-4717-9 ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:thm:weight-decomposition-exists","label":"thm:weight-decomposition-exists","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/weight-decomposition-exists.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.comp_idem_of_sum_id","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.comp_idem_of_sum_id","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/weight-decomposition-exists.lean#L79-L85","doc":"Auxiliary: given complementary idempotents summing to the identity,\nthe second projection is determined.  This is the key algebraic\nfact underlying the weight decomposition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WeightDecomposition.proj_V_idem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WeightDecomposition.proj_V_idem","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/weight-decomposition-exists.lean#L77-L77","doc":"Idempotency of vertical projection. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WeightDecomposition.proj_H_idem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WeightDecomposition.proj_H_idem","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/weight-decomposition-exists.lean#L75-L75","doc":"Idempotency of horizontal projection. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WeightDecomposition.complementary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WeightDecomposition.complementary","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/weight-decomposition-exists.lean#L73-L73","doc":"Complementarity: `π_H + π_V = id`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WeightDecomposition.proj_V","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WeightDecomposition.proj_V","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/weight-decomposition-exists.lean#L71-L71","doc":"The vertical projection `π_V` (non-zero weight). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WeightDecomposition.proj_H","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WeightDecomposition.proj_H","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/weight-decomposition-exists.lean#L69-L69","doc":"The horizontal projection `π_H` (weight-0). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WeightDecomposition.forms","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WeightDecomposition.forms","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/weight-decomposition-exists.lean#L67-L67","doc":"The object of `k`-forms `Ω^k(A)` in `C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WeightDecomposition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WeightDecomposition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/weight-decomposition-exists.lean#L64-L64","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WeightDecomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WeightDecomposition","kind":"structure","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/weight-decomposition-exists.lean#L59-L77","doc":"**Weight decomposition** (inlined from `def:weight-decomposition`):\nthe `T`-weight decomposition of differential forms into horizontal\n(weight-0) and vertical (non-zero weight) components.\n\nRef: [lusztig1993] https://doi.org/10.1007/978-0-8176-4717-9 ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:weight-decomposition","label":"def:weight-decomposition","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/weight-decomposition.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MaximalTorus.rank","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MaximalTorus.rank","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/weight-decomposition-exists.lean#L57-L57","doc":"**Maximality**: rank of the torus. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MaximalTorus.diagonal_action","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MaximalTorus.diagonal_action","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/weight-decomposition-exists.lean#L54-L54","doc":"**Diagonal action**: the image of `embed` is abelian. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MaximalTorus.embed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MaximalTorus.embed","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/weight-decomposition-exists.lean#L52-L52","doc":"The torus embeds into the gauge group. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MaximalTorus.torusGroup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MaximalTorus.torusGroup","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/weight-decomposition-exists.lean#L50-L50","doc":"The torus carries a group structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MaximalTorus.torusType","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MaximalTorus.torusType","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/weight-decomposition-exists.lean#L48-L48","doc":"The diagonal automorphism type (abstracting `T ≅ U(1)^r`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MaximalTorus.numWeights","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MaximalTorus.numWeights","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/weight-decomposition-exists.lean#L46-L46","doc":"The number of weight spaces of `V` under the torus action. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MaximalTorus.fibreFunctor_faithful","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MaximalTorus.fibreFunctor_faithful","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/weight-decomposition-exists.lean#L44-L44","doc":"**Faithfulness** of the fibre functor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MaximalTorus.fibreFunctor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MaximalTorus.fibreFunctor","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/weight-decomposition-exists.lean#L42-L42","doc":"The fibre functor `ω : C → Type*` (from the QOU). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MaximalTorus.V","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MaximalTorus.V","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/weight-decomposition-exists.lean#L40-L40","doc":"The fundamental object `V` of categorical dimension 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MaximalTorus.hopfObj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MaximalTorus.hopfObj","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/weight-decomposition-exists.lean#L38-L38","doc":"The Frobenius–Hopf object `A` in `C` (from the QOU). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MaximalTorus.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MaximalTorus.mk","kind":"ctor","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/weight-decomposition-exists.lean#L35-L35","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MaximalTorus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MaximalTorus","kind":"structure","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/weight-decomposition-exists.lean#L30-L57","doc":"**Maximal torus** (inlined from `def:maximal-torus`): the subgroup\nof `Aut⊗(ω)` acting diagonally on each weight space of the\nfundamental object `V`.\n\nRef: [lusztig1993] https://doi.org/10.1007/978-0-8176-4717-9 ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:maximal-torus","label":"def:maximal-torus","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/maximal-torus.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}